-- title:
--   Smooth Drinfeld charts on the descended full-level model, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime subject to `hq2 : q = 2`, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and a guard is imposed by the auxiliary level: a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of the Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by `jqModC` and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion substitute) over that residue field, and `hW` says that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` of supersingular places, that is, of places which are rational, affine-geometric, and whose evaluation of `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`. The hypothesis `hle` records the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of intermediate fields of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, the former being the base change to $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, the latter that of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`.
--
--   The reduction data are a constant reduction $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')` — a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the level-$M'$ field whose residue map onto the characteristic-$q$ function field is surjective with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with orders — and the hypothesis `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. An element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ is fixed, together with $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$.
--
--   Two families of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` are given: `OIg` indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), the projective line over $\mathbf{Z}/q$, and `OSS` indexed by $W$. (In `hIg` and `hIg_perm` the bound variable written `ℓ` ranges over [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) and shadows the prime $\ell$.) The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which describes `OIg (lineInfty q)` as the set of $f$ expressible as a quotient of coefficientwise images of Laurent series over $A$ with denominator of non-zero reduction; `hIg`, that every point of the projective line is $\mathrm{red}_q(\gamma) \cdot \infty$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `OIg` at that point the pullback of `OIg (lineInfty q)` along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of `OIg`; and `hIg_perm`, that for any $\zeta'$ and any $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family `OIg`.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that for each $s$ the elements of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ lying in `OSS s` are exactly those of $A$; `hSS_over`, which for $s \in W$ and $f$ in `R₀.integers` regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the image $\hat{j}$ of `jq` under `coeffEmb` is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, asserts both that the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OSS s` and that for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of that residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of `OSS s`; `hSS_fix`, that each `OSS s` is stable under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each `OSS s` contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of `OSS s` for every $a \in A$.
--
--   The descent data are: a subfield $K_0$ of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ with $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ algebraic over $K_0$ and $\pi \in K_0$; a ring $A_0$ which is a Henselian discrete valuation domain, an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ is exactly $A \cap K_0$ (`hιK₀`), with residue map $A_0 \to \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ surjective (`hres`), a generator $\varpi_0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ (`hϖ₀`) with $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$ (`hϖ₀π`); a subfield $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` characterised by `hF₀` as the set of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing $\hat{j}$ (`hjF₀`); and an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ whose structure map is $\iota$ followed by $\overline{\mathbf{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'` (`hj₀`).
--
--   The model data are: a scheme $X_0$ in universe $0$ with a morphism `toBase₀ : X₀ ⟶ Spec A₀` which is integral on the source and proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, all stalks being integrally closed (`hn₀`); a ring isomorphism $\varphi_0$ from $F_0$ to the function field of $X_0$ carrying the structure map of $A_0$ to `SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField toBase₀` (`hφ₀`); the relative-dimension-one condition `hdim`, that if $\eta$ lies over the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_0$ and is not closed, and $y$ is a specialisation of $\eta$ distinct from $\eta$, then $y$ is a closed point; and a dictionary `gen : CuspidalType.ProjLine q ⊕ ↥W → X₀` such that, writing `SemistableModel.localRing X₀ φ₀ x` for the subring of $F_0$ traced from the stalk at $x$, one has `localRing` at `gen (Sum.inl ℓ)` equal to the intersection of `OIg ℓ` with $F_0$ (`hgenIg`) and at `gen (Sum.inr s)` equal to the intersection of `OSS s` with $F_0$ (`hgenSS`), all points `gen i` lie over the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_0$ (`hgen₀`), and a point over the closed point is of the form `gen i` precisely when it is not closed (`hgen`). Finally $s \in W$ is fixed.
--
--   The conclusion is a conjunction of two assertions. First, `gen (Sum.inr s)` lies in the smooth locus of `toBase₀`.
--
--   Second, for every $x_0 \in X_0$ lying over the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_0$, closed (every specialisation of $x_0$ equals $x_0$), which is a specialisation of `gen (Sum.inr s)` and of no `gen (Sum.inl ℓ)` for $\ell$ in the projective line, there exist an $A_0$-subalgebra $B$ of $F_0$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of $B$ such that all of the following hold: $B$ is finitely generated as an $A_0$-algebra; $B$ is integrally closed in $F_0$, every $x \in F_0$ integral over $B$ lying in $B$; $F_0$ is the fraction field of $B$, every $x \in F_0$ satisfying $xc = b$ with $b, c \in B$, $c \neq 0$; every prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of $B$ containing the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ and not maximal is a minimal prime of that image; for every non-zero prime $\mathfrak{p}$ of $B$ not containing the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ there is a valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ whose elements are exactly the $f$ with $fc = b$ for some $b, c \in B$, $c \notin \mathfrak{p}$, i.e. the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{p}$ is a valuation ring; for every non-closed point $\eta$ over the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_0$ with $B$ contained in `SemistableModel.localRing X₀ φ₀ η` there is a prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of $B$ such that that local ring is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{q}$, described by the same quotient condition; conversely, for every minimal prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ in $B$ there is a non-closed point $\eta$ over the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_0$ whose traced local ring is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{q}$; the element $\hat{j}$, viewed in $F_0$ via `hjF₀`, lies in $B$; $B$ is contained in `SemistableModel.localRing X₀ φ₀ (gen i)` only for $i =$ `Sum.inr s`; the traced local ring of $X_0$ at $x_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{m}$, again in the quotient form; and the structure map from $A_0$ to `Localization.AtPrime 𝔪` is formally smooth.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case, at a rigid auxiliary level $M'$ with an auxiliary prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the Drinfeld-neighbourhood step for the descended full-level modular curve: the supersingular (Drinfeld) component of the special fibre of the normal proper flat model $X_0$ over the tame base $A_0$ is shown to be smooth at its generic point, and every closed special point lying on that component and on no Igusa component is shown to admit a normal finitely generated affine chart, centred on that component alone, containing $j$, whose localisation at the point is formally smooth over $A_0$. It feeds the construction of the semistable scheme over the descent base from the given families of valuation subrings, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableScheme_over_descentBase_of_valuationSubrings_of_eq_pi_relDimOne_jDich_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableScheme_over_descentBase_of_valuationSubrings_of_eq_pi_relDimOne_jDich_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
